{%- comment -%}
  Mirrors ../design-system/src/react/ProductCard/ProductCardActions.tsx plus the Button it wraps:
  the action row at the foot of a product card. ProductCard.md's example is
  `<ProductCardActions><Button variant="primary" size="sm">Afegir a la cistella</Button></ProductCardActions>`.

  It deliberately does NOT reproduce .actions's box geometry from ProductCard.module.css:34-38. That
  rule's padding is now four merchant padding settings defaulting to 0 -- see the stylesheet -- so the
  block imposes no inset and the composition decides. Only margin-block-start: auto is kept, which is
  what puts the row at the foot of the card.

  It is a direct child block of Horizon's native blocks/_product-card.liquid, a sibling of
  mionas-price rather than nested in a _product-card-group row. It reads closest.product and renders
  nothing without one, and unlike a
  private block it is NOT hidden from the picker: a merchant adds and orders it in the theme
  editor, so it needs to appear there.

  WHY THIS IS A BLOCK AND NOT A RESKIN of blocks/add-to-cart.liquid:
  that block's own doc header says can_add_to_cart and add_to_cart_text are parameters "intended for
  product-form.liquid block" -- they arrive from the parent block, not from settings, so it cannot
  render standalone inside a card. There is no schema path to give it a product context either.

  WHY IT DOES NOT RENDER snippets/quick-add.liquid, whose branch logic below is otherwise copied
  from it (quick-add.liquid:11-58):
  quick-add.liquid renders snippets/quick-add-styles.liquid, which makes .quick-add absolutely
  positioned over the card at opacity 0 until the card is hovered, and .quick-add__button a
  fixed-size round pill anchored to the media's bottom-right corner
  (quick-add-styles.liquid:17-107). That is Horizon's floating-pill pattern; the design system's is
  a static full-row action. There is no setting or class that opts out, so this block emits the same
  structure and the same data-* attributes assets/quick-add.js reads, under its own class names, and
  leaves quick-add-styles.liquid unrendered.

  WHY THE BUTTON STILL COMES FROM snippets/add-to-cart-button.liquid:
  that snippet is the <add-to-cart-component> wrapper, the checkmark-burst markup and the
  ref="addToCartButton" binding that drive the added-to-cart animation and the fly-to-cart flight.
  Reproducing it here would fork behaviour that upstream still maintains.

  WHY THE BUTTON WEARS blocks/mionas-button.liquid's CLASSES RATHER THAN ITS OWN:
  mionas-button.liquid already spends every --button-* token in the shape the design system's Button
  does, so this block hands the snippet `mionas-button mionas-button--<variant>` and declares no
  button styling of its own. mionas-button.liquid itself cannot be composed here -- it renders an <a>
  with a `link` setting and has no way to submit a form -- but its stylesheet is exactly what this
  button needs, and reusing the classes keeps one button implementation instead of two that must be
  kept in step by hand.

  Two things make that safe, both verified against the running dev server rather than assumed:

  1. The snippet prefixes whatever class attribute it is handed with a literal "button", so the
     button also carries Horizon's .button (base.css:1006-1040). Both .button and .mionas-button are
     single-class selectors, so specificity ties and source order decides -- and it is decided
     structurally: base.css is its own <link> in the head, while every block stylesheet tag lands
     in compiled_assets/styles.css, which the theme links afterwards. .mionas-button therefore wins.
  2. compiled_assets/styles.css is served with a `subset` query parameter, which reads as though a
     block's CSS might be dropped on pages where that block does not render -- which would leave this
     button unstyled anywhere mionas-button is absent. It does not: the file is byte-identical on the
     home page, /cart and a collection page, and .mionas-button--primary is present in all three.

  Two button rules are left in this file, both because .add-to-cart-button declares the same
  properties from an equally specific selector and would win on bundle order: the pressed state and
  the height. Both are documented at the point of declaration.

  WHY THE CHOOSE-OPTIONS BRANCH CAN FALL BACK TO A LINK:
  the quick-add dialog is a single global element, rendered in layout/theme.liquid:185-187 only when
  settings.quick_add or settings.mobile_quick_add is on. settings.quick_add defaults to true
  (config/settings_schema.json:1852-1854), but config/settings_data.json now sets it explicitly to
  false, so the dialog is currently absent and every multi-variant product takes this fallback
  branch, not the quick-add one below -- a merchant can switch it back on, and then the choose
  button would open nothing if this branch were the only one. Rendering a second dialog per card is
  not an option: they would collide on the #quick-add-dialog id that quick-add.js:134 looks up. So
  the fallback is a plain link to the product page, styled identically.

  WHY THE VARIANT SETTING OFFERS FOUR OF mionas-button.liquid's SEVEN:
  the class vocabulary is shared, but the schema deliberately is not. danger and the two inverse
  variants exist for destructive actions and dark grounds. A product card is a white card with a
  non-destructive primary action, so those three would only ever be misconfigurations here. Add them
  if a dark card variant ever lands -- the CSS for them already exists.

  ONE KNOWN COSMETIC OVERLAP: pressing this button also dims the whole card, because
  snippets/product-card-bridge.liquid:43's `.product-card:active .product-card__content { opacity: ... }`
  matches on ancestors of the pressed element. Left as-is rather than scoping the card's pressed
  state around this block.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign product = closest.product
-%}

{%- if product != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign block_settings = block.settings
    assign selected_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
    assign product_form_id = 'MionasAddToCart-' | append: product.id | append: '-' | append: block.id

    assign uses_selling_plans = false
    if product.requires_selling_plan or product.selling_plan_groups.size > 0
      assign uses_selling_plans = true
    endif

    assign can_add_to_cart = false
    if selected_variant.available
      assign can_add_to_cart = true
    endif

    comment
      Each label falls back to the locale string the native path uses -- 'actions.add' and
      'actions.choose' from quick-add.liquid:12-13, 'products.product.sold_out' from
      buy-buttons.liquid:30 -- so a block left alone stays translated with the rest of the theme, and
      a merchant who types a label gets exactly that.

      `| default:` is not enough on its own here: a text setting the merchant has cleared comes back
      as an empty string, and default only substitutes for nil or false. Hence the blank checks.
    endcomment
    assign add_to_cart_text = block_settings.label_add
    if add_to_cart_text == blank
      assign add_to_cart_text = 'actions.add' | t
    endif

    unless can_add_to_cart
      assign add_to_cart_text = block_settings.label_sold_out
      if add_to_cart_text == blank
        assign add_to_cart_text = 'products.product.sold_out' | t
      endif
    endunless

    assign choose_options_text = block_settings.label_choose
    if choose_options_text == blank
      assign choose_options_text = 'actions.choose' | t
    endif

    comment
      Only a single-variant product resolves to one variant at render time, so only it gets a real
      add-to-cart form. Everything else -- multiple options, and selling plans regardless of variant
      count, since subscription widgets only run on the product page -- goes to the choose branch.
      quick-add.liquid additionally renders both buttons for a single-option swatch product, because
      a swatch click there can resolve the variant client-side and flip choose -> add. Mionas cards
      render no swatches, so that case cannot arise and is not reproduced.
    endcomment
    assign render_add = false
    if product.variants_count == 1 and uses_selling_plans == false
      assign render_add = true
    endif

    assign quick_add_modal_available = false
    if settings.quick_add or settings.mobile_quick_add
      assign quick_add_modal_available = true
    endif

    assign style_variant = block_settings.variant | default: 'primary'
    assign size = block_settings.size | default: 'md'

    comment
      Same class vocabulary blocks/mionas-button.liquid builds, in the same order, so that block's
      stylesheet does all the work here. add-to-cart-button is Horizon's own hook for the
      checkmark-burst and fly-to-cart animation CSS (add-to-cart-button-styles.liquid) and has to
      stay on regardless of variant.
    endcomment
    assign button_classes = 'add-to-cart-button mionas-button mionas-button--' | append: style_variant
    unless size == 'md'
      assign button_classes = button_classes | append: ' mionas-button--' | append: size
    endunless
    if block_settings.full_width
      assign button_classes = button_classes | append: ' mionas-button--full'
    endif

    comment
      The icon is hidden with a class rather than by not rendering it. snippets/add-to-cart-button.liquid
      emits the cart icon unconditionally whenever can_add_to_cart and takes no parameter for it, so the
      alternatives were to fork that snippet -- giving up the <add-to-cart-component> wrapper, the
      ref binding and the checkmark-burst markup it exists to provide -- or to switch it off in CSS.
      CSS wins: the icon is decorative and already aria-hidden, so display: none removes it from the
      accessibility tree too and nothing is announced that is not shown.

      The modifier sits on the wrapper, not the button, so that one class governs both the cart icon
      in the add branch and the plus icon the choose and fallback branches emit under icon_only --
      the shared button_classes would otherwise have to carry a toggle that means something different
      per branch.

      show_icon and icon_only are mutually exclusive above rather than additive: show_icon is
      visible_if'd off in the editor when icon_only is on, but a stored false survives that, and both
      modifiers together would render a button with neither icon nor label.
    endcomment
    assign wrapper_classes = 'mionas-add-to-cart'
    if block_settings.icon_only
      assign wrapper_classes = wrapper_classes | append: ' mionas-add-to-cart--icon-only'
    elsif block_settings.show_icon == false
      assign wrapper_classes = wrapper_classes | append: ' mionas-add-to-cart--no-icon'
    endif
  -%}

  {% render 'add-to-cart-button-styles' %}
  {% render 'fly-to-cart-styles' %}

  <div
    class="{{ wrapper_classes }} spacing-style"
    style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: block_settings %}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    {%- if render_add -%}
      <product-form-component
        data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
        data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
        on:submit="/handleSubmit"
      >
        {%- comment -%}
          ProductFormComponent.requiredRefs is ['variantId', 'liveRegion'] (product-form.js:206) --
          the component does not initialise without both, so neither the hidden input's ref nor this
          region is optional.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div
          class="visually-hidden"
          aria-live="assertive"
          role="status"
          aria-atomic="true"
          ref="liveRegion"
        ></div>
        {%- form 'product', product, id: product_form_id, novalidate: 'novalidate', data-type: 'add-to-cart-form' -%}
          <input
            type="hidden"
            name="id"
            ref="variantId"
            value="{{ selected_variant.id }}"
            {% if can_add_to_cart == false %}
              disabled
            {% endif %}
          >
          <input
            type="hidden"
            name="quantity"
            value="{% if selected_variant.quantity_rule.min %}{{ selected_variant.quantity_rule.min }}{% else %}1{% endif %}"
          >
          {%- if block_settings.icon_only and can_add_to_cart == false -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              snippets/add-to-cart-button.liquid:41-47 only emits its icon span when can_add_to_cart,
              so a sold-out product gets no icon from that snippet -- and the icon-only stylesheet
              rule's font-size: 0 then collapses the "Agotado" label too, leaving a blank disabled
              square. Verified on the dev server: 2 of 24 cards on /collections/comprar-cookies.

              Bypassing the snippet here is safe specifically because this branch is disabled: the
              <add-to-cart-component> wrapper, the ref="addToCartButton" binding and the
              checkmark-burst markup all exist to drive the added-to-cart animation, and a disabled
              button can never fire it. Nothing that snippet provides is given up.

              Only reached under icon_only -- in text mode the sold-out label is visible on its own
              and there is nothing to fix.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              The literal "button" class below is what base.css:1078-1081's .button:disabled
              { opacity: 0.5; cursor: not-allowed; } hooks onto. snippets/add-to-cart-button.liquid:33
              supplies it for free on the other path (class="button {{ class }}"), but this branch
              bypasses that snippet, so it has to be added by hand or a sold-out card would render
              indistinguishable from a buyable one apart from the glyph.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <button
              class="button {{ button_classes }}"
              type="submit"
              name="add"
              disabled
            >
              <span class="svg-wrapper" aria-hidden="true">
                {{- 'icon-unavailable.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
              </span>
              {{- add_to_cart_text -}}
            </button>
          {%- else -%}
            {% render 'add-to-cart-button',
              add_to_cart_text: add_to_cart_text,
              class: button_classes,
              can_add_to_cart: can_add_to_cart,
              product: product
            %}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endform -%}
      </product-form-component>
    {%- elsif quick_add_modal_available -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        QuickAddComponent finds the product URL through this.closest('product-card') and that
        element's refs.productCardLink (quick-add.js:16-19, product-card.js:110-124). Horizon's own
        snippets/product-card.liquid:62,88 supplies both -- a <product-card> element whose overlay
        link carries ref="productCardLink" -- so this button works wherever that card renders it.
        Without both, it would open an empty dialog.

        data-quick-add-button is fixed at 'choose' and data-renders-both-buttons is omitted, so
        QuickAddComponent's productSelect handler returns early (quick-add.js:66) instead of
        flipping to a nonexistent add button.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <quick-add-component
        class="mionas-add-to-cart__quick-add"
        data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
        data-quick-add-button="choose"
        data-product-options-count="{{ product.options.size }}"
        data-uses-selling-plans="{{ uses_selling_plans }}"
      >
        {%- comment -%}
          type="button" is explicit: submit is the default, and QuickAddComponent opens a dialog
          rather than submitting anything. Same reasoning as quick-add.liquid:127.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The add branch gets its icon free from snippets/add-to-cart-button.liquid:41-47. These two
          branches build their own markup and have never had one, so icon_only has to supply it or
          the font-size: 0 rule below would leave an empty box. Only rendered under icon_only, so
          text mode looks exactly as it did.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <button
          class="{{ button_classes }}"
          type="button"
          name="add"
          on:click="quick-add-component/handleClick"
        >
          {%- if block_settings.icon_only -%}
            <span class="svg-wrapper" aria-hidden="true">
              {{- 'icon-plus.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
          {{- choose_options_text -}}
        </button>
      </quick-add-component>
    {%- else -%}
      <a class="{{ button_classes }}" href="{{ product.url }}">
        {%- if block_settings.icon_only -%}
          <span class="svg-wrapper" aria-hidden="true">
            {{- 'icon-plus.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {{- choose_options_text -}}
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /* NO PADDING IS DECLARED HERE ON PURPOSE. This used to carry
     padding-block-start: var(--product-card-base-gap) and
     padding-inline: var(--product-card-base-padding-inline), mirroring .actions in
     ProductCard.module.css:34-38. Both are gone: padding is now four range settings rendered through
     snippets/spacing-style.liquid, defaulting to 0, so the block imposes no inset of its own and the
     composition decides. That is the same mechanism, and the same four setting ids, that Horizon's
     own blocks/_product-card.liquid exposes for the card itself.

     Note the block still sits in a flex `gap`, so removing padding-block-start does not collapse the
     space above the button -- the button is a direct child of blocks/_product-card.liquid, a sibling
     of mionas-price, product-title and mionas-product-description (no _product-card-group wraps it),
     so the separation above it comes from the card's own product_card_gap setting
     (_product-card.liquid), not a group-level token. The horizontal inset is set on this block
     itself: both templates that place it, templates/index.json and templates/collection.json,
     configure padding-inline-start/end to 16 here, not 0, so the button does not run to the card's
     edges. That value lives in the theme editor per instance, same as any other padding this block
     leaves unset above.

     margin-block-start: auto is NOT padding and stays. It pins the action row to the card's foot so
     buttons line up across a grid row however the titles wrap. */
  .mionas-add-to-cart {
    margin-block-start: auto;
  }

  /* Set when the Show icon setting is off. Targets snippets/add-to-cart-button.liquid's own icon
     span, which is the only icon in the rendered button, and which that snippet marks aria-hidden --
     so display: none takes it out of the layout and the a11y tree consistently. The gap between icon
     and label is mionas-button.liquid's `gap`, which collapses on its own with one child left. */
  .mionas-add-to-cart--no-icon .add-to-cart-icon {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Icon-only mode. font-size: 0 is what collapses the label: add-to-cart-button.liquid:48 emits it
     as a bare text node with no element to select, so there is nothing to put display: none on. The
     node stays in the accessibility tree, which is the point -- it remains the button's accessible
     name and no aria-label is needed.

     The icon survives a zero font-size because .svg-wrapper is sized from --icon-size-sm, which is
     1.25rem (theme-styles-variables.liquid:549) -- rem, not em. .mionas-button declares no gap
     either, so nothing else collapses.

     (0,2,0) on purpose: .mionas-button, .mionas-button--sm and .mionas-button--lg each declare
     padding and font-size at one class, and this has to outrank whichever size is selected.
     aspect-ratio squares the button against the height those same rules set, so it tracks the size
     token instead of naming a width. Note --full still wins on width if a merchant sets both; that
     combination is a misconfiguration, not a supported mode. */
  .mionas-add-to-cart--icon-only .mionas-button {
    font-size: 0;
    padding-inline: 0;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
  }

  .mionas-add-to-cart__quick-add {
    display: block;
  }

  /* The pressed state is the one place the two stylesheets genuinely collide, and it is not a
     specificity problem -- it is a different-property problem that no source order resolves.
     mionas-button.liquid presses with `transform: scale(...)`, while .add-to-cart-button:active
     presses with `scale` and `translate` (add-to-cart-button-styles.liquid). Those are separate
     properties, so both apply and the button shrinks twice and drifts down a pixel.

     Zeroing Horizon's two properties here, at (0,2,0) so it wins outright, leaves mionas-button's
     transform and opacity as the only pressed state -- which is the point of wearing its classes.
     The button keeps .add-to-cart-button because the checkmark-burst and fly-to-cart CSS hangs off
     it; this rule is the cost of that. */
  .mionas-add-to-cart .mionas-button:active {
    scale: 1;
    translate: none;
  }

  /* The second collision, and the same shape as the one above: .add-to-cart-button declares
     `height: var(--height-buy-buttons)` (52px, the product page's buy-button height), which ties with
     .mionas-button's own height at one class each and wins on bundle order. Measured, not assumed --
     the button rendered 52px tall next to a 48px Mionas button.

     So the height is re-asserted here at (0,2,0), one rule per size, which is the only part of
     mionas-button.liquid's sizing this file has to repeat. Everything else it declares -- padding,
     font-size, radius, colours -- .add-to-cart-button does not touch, so it comes through untouched.
     If mionas-button.liquid ever gains a size, add it here too. */
  .mionas-add-to-cart .mionas-button {
    height: var(--button-size-md-height);
  }

  .mionas-add-to-cart .mionas-button--sm {
    height: var(--button-size-sm-height);
  }

  .mionas-add-to-cart .mionas-button--lg {
    height: var(--button-size-lg-height);
  }

  /* mionas-button.liquid only ever renders an <a>, so it styles [aria-disabled="true"] and has no
     :disabled rule. A sold-out product here is a real disabled <button>, which needs the same
     token. */
  .mionas-add-to-cart .mionas-button:disabled {
    opacity: var(--button-state-disabled-opacity);
    cursor: default;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Mionas: Add to cart",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Text"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label_add",
      "label": "Add to cart label",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the theme's own wording, which stays translated per language."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label_choose",
      "label": "Choose options label",
      "info": "Shown on products with more than one variant, which open the variant picker instead of adding straight away."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label_sold_out",
      "label": "Sold out label"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Icon"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "icon_only",
      "label": "Icon only",
      "info": "Hides the label and shows only the icon. The label stays as the button's accessible name, so screen readers still announce it.",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_icon",
      "label": "Show cart icon",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Only the add-to-cart button has an icon; the choose-options button never does.",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_only == false }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Style"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "variant",
      "label": "Variant",
      "options": [
        { "value": "primary", "label": "Primary" },
        { "value": "secondary", "label": "Secondary" },
        { "value": "outline", "label": "Outline" },
        { "value": "ghost", "label": "Ghost" }
      ],
      "default": "primary"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "size",
      "label": "Size",
      "options": [
        { "value": "sm", "label": "Small" },
        { "value": "md", "label": "Medium" },
        { "value": "lg", "label": "Large" }
      ],
      "default": "md"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "full_width",
      "label": "Full width",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "t:settings.top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "t:settings.bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-inline-start",
      "label": "t:settings.left",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-inline-end",
      "label": "t:settings.right",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Mionas: Add to cart",
      "category": "t:categories.product"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
